# Line endings.
#
# Git is configured with autocrlf here: it stores LF and checks out CRLF. That
# is harmless for Python, and fatal for anything the container executes
# directly. `docker build` copies from the working tree rather than from git, so
# a checked-out entrypoint.sh carries CRLF into the image, the shebang becomes
# `#!/bin/sh\r`, and the container exits with "no such file or directory" — a
# failure that says nothing about line endings and does not reproduce on Linux.
#
# The last matching pattern wins, so the general rule comes first.

* text=auto

# Executed inside a Linux container: LF in the working tree, not just in git.
*.sh                 text eol=lf
Dockerfile           text eol=lf
*.dockerfile         text eol=lf
docker-compose*.yml  text eol=lf
.dockerignore        text eol=lf
